      "seed": 850945168,
      "version": 841,
      "versionNonce": 68026762,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1769924373372,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "## **Round 4: High-Level Design (TempMail Service)**\n\n**Topic:**\n\nDesign a **TempMail generation service** where generated emails are valid for **5\nhours**.\n\nDiscussion focused on:\n\n- Expiry mechanism\n- Storage strategies\n- Access control and validation\n- Building sensible mail names",
      "fontSize": 46.687104048623496,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "## **Round 4: High-Level Design (TempMail Service)**\n\n**Topic:**\n\nDesign a **TempMail generation service** where generated emails are valid for **5 hours**.\n\nDiscussion focused on:\n\n- Expiry mechanism\n- Storage strategies\n- Access control and validation\n- Building sensible mail names",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "FJDVqJo--YUmYQv4Diu4-",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1908.7882753419794,
      "y": 10483.03373988526,
      "width": 1288.0435791015625,
      "height": 3285,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aH",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1078756464,
      "version": 1441,
      "versionNonce": 217330710,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1769924373372,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "FR: \n- user should be able to generate temp email. kind of temp email website.\n- and will expire in 5h \n- do we need to show inbox ? -> YES\n\n- what about domain ?? -> any domain doesn't matter\n\n\nflow: \n    - user generate email id \n    - user user those email for signup etc\n    - what ever inbox it will get will show on screen.\n    - what if user refreshes page ? \n    \n\nNFR: \n    - can user generate as many email as possible ?  -> x/10min -> 5/10min\n    - rate limiting -> can user generate another after refresh ? \n    - after 5h permanent delete ? \n    - pager and monitorings.\n    - scalable \n    - durability\n    - consistency\n    - security\n    - availability\n    - cost\n    \n\n\nEstimations: \n    - QPs -> \n    - peak qps \n\n\nEntities: \n    - User\n    - GeneratedEmail \n    - Inbox\n    - UserGeneratedEmail\n    - GmailIntegration\n\nApi design: \n    \n1. for generating the email \n    /api/v1/tempemail/generate GET \nx-token -> for verification\ncontain userId \n\nResponse: \n{\n  status code: <> \n  email id : <> \n}\n\n2. for fetching inboxes in pagination \n\n  /api/v1/tempemail/fetchinboxes ? pageSize = 10 && offset = 10. GET\n\nResponse: {\n    status code: <> \n    pageSize : <>. \n    offset: <> \n    hasNext: <>\n    inboxes: [{\n        {Inbox1}, {Inbox2}....\n    }]\n}\n\nnext page\n    pageSize = 10 \n    offset = 20 \n\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "FR: \n- user should be able to generate temp email. kind of temp email website.\n- and will expire in 5h \n- do we need to show inbox ? -> YES\n\n- what about domain ?? -> any domain doesn't matter\n\n\nflow: \n    - user generate email id \n    - user user those email for signup etc\n    - what ever inbox it will get will show on screen.\n    - what if user refreshes page ? \n    \n\nNFR: \n    - can user generate as many email as possible ?  -> x/10min -> 5/10min\n    - rate limiting -> can user generate another after refresh ? \n    - after 5h permanent delete ? \n    - pager and monitorings.\n    - scalable \n    - durability\n    - consistency\n    - security\n    - availability\n    - cost\n    \n\n\nEstimations: \n    - QPs -> \n    - peak qps \n\n\nEntities: \n    - User\n    - GeneratedEmail \n    - Inbox\n    - UserGeneratedEmail\n    - GmailIntegration\n\nApi design: \n    \n1. for generating the email \n    /api/v1/tempemail/generate GET \nx-token -> for verification\ncontain userId \n\nResponse: \n{\n  status code: <> \n  email id : <> \n}\n\n2. for fetching inboxes in pagination \n\n  /api/v1/tempemail/fetchinboxes ? pageSize = 10 && offset = 10. GET\n\nResponse: {\n    status code: <> \n    pageSize : <>. \n    offset: <> \n    hasNext: <>\n    inboxes: [{\n        {Inbox1}, {Inbox2}....\n    }]\n}\n\nnext page\n    pageSize = 10 \n    offset = 20 \n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ae6FE6CyLScel5qXzwIuT",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -176.69943643193847,
      "y": 10361.250707226332,
      "width": 1018.3676147460938,
      "height": 1350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "aI",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1379662402,
      "version": 1346,
      "versionNonce": 313081930,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1769924373372,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "HLD -> 1. functional requirements -> nFR \n\n\n\nAssumption: -> third party for email creation\n       let say it require only email for email genreate\n       not name etc. \n\n\nSolution: \n\nwe can buy the domains as per our qps\nlet say 500 domains. \n\nand register to DNS ( usually email works similar \nto how website domain works, there is smtp server\nwhich uses smtp protocol to send the message to thsi\nemail , then system send this to dns, it return the smtp\nserver ip for that domain like gmail.com, mindtickle.com etc\nso gmail.com email will go to google smtp server, then\nthey pass to their internal server and save inboxes\nand on gmail ui it fetches from those internal servers. ) \nso similar to this we can by domains. \n\nnow we'll generated random email -> ask for account\ncreation \n\n{random}@{out of those domain}.com \n\nafter 5 hours , we'll delete that account. ",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "HLD -> 1. functional requirements -> nFR \n\n\n\nAssumption: -> third party for email creation\n       let say it require only email for email genreate\n       not name etc. \n\n\nSolution: \n\nwe can buy the domains as per our qps\nlet say 500 domains. \n\nand register to DNS ( usually email works similar \nto how website domain works, there is smtp server\nwhich uses smtp protocol to send the message to thsi\nemail , then system send this to dns, it return the smtp\nserver ip for that domain like gmail.com, mindtickle.com etc\nso gmail.com email will go to google smtp server, then\nthey pass to their internal server and save inboxes\nand on gmail ui it fetches from those internal servers. ) \nso similar to this we can by domains. \n\nnow we'll generated random email -> ask for account\ncreation \n\n{random}@{out of those domain}.com \n\nafter 5 hours , we'll delete that account. ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
