      "updated": 1769924373372,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1.  Design a system like Feedly. Focus on API design and data modeling for\nsubscribing/unsubscribing and newsfeed generation. ( RSS feed ) ",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1.  Design a system like Feedly. Focus on API design and data modeling for subscribing/unsubscribing and newsfeed generation. ( RSS feed ) ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "TdJb8JJodBJVHyb5ohoLR",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6224.955307423694,
      "y": 9686.707399959618,
      "width": 1189.3555908203125,
      "height": 3465,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b1b",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1347004694,
      "version": 2591,
      "versionNonce": 616317398,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1769925293783,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "FR: \n- Users can subscribe/unsubscribe to RSS feeds or sources.\n- Users can see a newsfeed of recent articles from the feeds they follow.\n- Users can mark articles as read/unread.\n- Users can organize feeds into categories.\n- User can also go in particular rss and see their all feeds.\n\nout of scope:\n- user some how subscribe that rss, not implement seraching rss etc. \n\nrss ingestion: \n-> feedly system offline find the RSS or admin add the RSS explicitly\n-> like admin added netflix engineer blog rss -> user can subscribe this. \n-> whenever new things added in this blog, feedly system receive it \n    -> asssume it can be via api or via subscritiponi\n\nExample: Every 10 minutes, fetch https://techcrunch.com/feed/ and parse new articles.\nor some also support via webhook etc as ofn ow assume first one. \n\nflow -> Ingestion \n      -> subscription\n      -> feed \n      -> categorisation\n      -> read/unread default category\n\n\nNFR: \n- Scalable. \n- deduplication of rss feed some how. \n- retention -? -> upto 6 month old else delete from our system\n- fine with bit delay from actual publish. \n- feed -> chronological order + alphabetical order. \n- alerts and monitoring and logging \n- high available system and fault tolerant. \n- polling -> rate limiting. \n\n\nEntities: \n\n- User \n- RssFeed -> netflix engg blog\n- RssFeedArticles -> \"How netflix implemented search engine, Deep dive\" \n- Subscription etc. \n- UserFeed \n- UserRssFeedCategory \n\n\nApi design: \n\nUser perspective\n\n-> service-service => grpc\n    else can use https;\n\n1.  subscribe/unsubscribe \n\n     /api/v1/feed/subscribe? id=<>\n     /api/v1/feed/unsubscribe? id=<>\n    \n    GET\n    \n    x-token, x-request-id, etc \n    \n    Response: { statusCode: 4xx,5xx,2xx. }\n    \n2. /api/v1/feed/user/{userId}? pageSize=<> &&offset=<> \n\n    GET\n    \n    x-token, x-request-id \n\n    Response: {\n      pageSize: <> \n      offset: <> \n      articles: [\n            {article1},{article2}......   // will see in db schema\n        ]\n   }\n\n 3. /api/v1/feed/read ? id=\"\"           // PUT\n    /api/v1/feed/unread ? id=\"\"         // PUT\n\n4. /api/v1/feed/addlabel ? id =\"\" && label =\"\"  // PUT\n\n\n admin perspetive\n\n5. /api/v1/feed       POST\n\nRequest: { feedData }\nResponse: {statusCode:<> }\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "FR: \n- Users can subscribe/unsubscribe to RSS feeds or sources.\n- Users can see a newsfeed of recent articles from the feeds they follow.\n- Users can mark articles as read/unread.\n- Users can organize feeds into categories.\n- User can also go in particular rss and see their all feeds.\n\nout of scope:\n- user some how subscribe that rss, not implement seraching rss etc. \n\nrss ingestion: \n-> feedly system offline find the RSS or admin add the RSS explicitly\n-> like admin added netflix engineer blog rss -> user can subscribe this. \n-> whenever new things added in this blog, feedly system receive it \n    -> asssume it can be via api or via subscritiponi\n\nExample: Every 10 minutes, fetch https://techcrunch.com/feed/ and parse new articles.\nor some also support via webhook etc as ofn ow assume first one. \n\nflow -> Ingestion \n      -> subscription\n      -> feed \n      -> categorisation\n      -> read/unread default category\n\n\nNFR: \n- Scalable. \n- deduplication of rss feed some how. \n- retention -? -> upto 6 month old else delete from our system\n- fine with bit delay from actual publish. \n- feed -> chronological order + alphabetical order. \n- alerts and monitoring and logging \n- high available system and fault tolerant. \n- polling -> rate limiting. \n\n\nEntities: \n\n- User \n- RssFeed -> netflix engg blog\n- RssFeedArticles -> \"How netflix implemented search engine, Deep dive\" \n- Subscription etc. \n- UserFeed \n- UserRssFeedCategory \n\n\nApi design: \n\nUser perspective\n\n-> service-service => grpc\n    else can use https;\n\n1.  subscribe/unsubscribe \n\n     /api/v1/feed/subscribe? id=<>\n     /api/v1/feed/unsubscribe? id=<>\n    \n    GET\n    \n    x-token, x-request-id, etc \n    \n    Response: { statusCode: 4xx,5xx,2xx. }\n    \n2. /api/v1/feed/user/{userId}? pageSize=<> &&offset=<> \n\n    GET\n    \n    x-token, x-request-id \n\n    Response: {\n      pageSize: <> \n      offset: <> \n      articles: [\n            {article1},{article2}......   // will see in db schema\n        ]\n   }\n\n 3. /api/v1/feed/read ? id=\"\"           // PUT\n    /api/v1/feed/unread ? id=\"\"         // PUT\n\n4. /api/v1/feed/addlabel ? id =\"\" && label =\"\"  // PUT\n\n\n admin perspetive\n\n5. /api/v1/feed       POST\n\nRequest: { feedData }\nResponse: {statusCode:<> }\n\n \n\n\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
