      "id": "9hc_tTfr6Aa-lUVFgWqmq",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 11498.850317503979,
      "y": 10446.948758473725,
      "width": 775.0794677734375,
      "height": 325,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b57",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 316072854,
      "version": 73,
      "versionNonce": 1495207626,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1769930485935,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "High level design and solution . \n\n\n-> we can have couple of service\n    -> dataplane -> for the users .\n    -> controlplan -> for the controlling of clusters or nodes broker etc. \n            -> data plane use this to find, the nodes url etc. \n\n\n-> kafka -> list of nodes -> broker -> different data centre\n-> replication factor etc. \nassuming we have install kafka and up that system and its running -> not going\ninto this.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "High level design and solution . \n\n\n-> we can have couple of service\n    -> dataplane -> for the users .\n    -> controlplan -> for the controlling of clusters or nodes broker etc. \n            -> data plane use this to find, the nodes url etc. \n\n\n-> kafka -> list of nodes -> broker -> different data centre\n-> replication factor etc. \nassuming we have install kafka and up that system and its running -> not going into this.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "oKdf_U8XpUk1JZZTWEsKA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 9980.511543984609,
      "y": 9932.41451139981,
      "width": 681.7196044921875,
      "height": 925,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b58",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2016540426,
      "version": 603,
      "versionNonce": 1524519126,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1769937844704,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Apis design: \n\n1. CRUD apis for node addition, remove, updation etc.\n2. CRUD for cluster addition \n2. CRUS apis for tenant node addition, updation etc. \n\n\nDb design: \n\n let say for kafka to be working we need list of node endpoint or url \n\n\n0. Cluster: \n    - id \n    - nodeCounts\n    - creationTime\n    - createdBy\n\n1. Nodes: \n    - id \n    - region // ap-south, ap-southeast etc // assume aws using \n    - addedTime\n    - addedBy\n    - endPoint. \n    - clusterId \n\n1 node : m tenants\n\n2.  TenantNodes: \n\n    - id \n    - tenantId\n    - clusterId \n    - addedTime \n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Apis design: \n\n1. CRUD apis for node addition, remove, updation etc.\n2. CRUD for cluster addition \n2. CRUS apis for tenant node addition, updation etc. \n\n\nDb design: \n\n let say for kafka to be working we need list of node endpoint or url \n\n\n0. Cluster: \n    - id \n    - nodeCounts\n    - creationTime\n    - createdBy\n\n1. Nodes: \n    - id \n    - region // ap-south, ap-southeast etc // assume aws using \n    - addedTime\n    - addedBy\n    - endPoint. \n    - clusterId \n\n1 node : m tenants\n\n2.  TenantNodes: \n\n    - id \n    - tenantId\n    - clusterId \n    - addedTime \n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
